    <worksheet name='Q4 '>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Q4. What insight can be gained by comparing Sales and Profit together? 
Then explain how you would create a chart to analyze Profit by Sub-Category.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources />
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style />
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Automatic' />
          </pane>
        </panes>
        <rows />
        <cols />
        <annotations>
          <annotation class='area' id='0' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Insight from Comparing Sales and Profit Together
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Sales alone</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> shows how much revenue is generated, but it doesn’t reveal whether the company is actually making money.
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Profit</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> accounts for costs and discounts, showing the true financial health.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>By comparing both, you can identify:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>&gt;&gt; Categories or products with </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>high sales but low/negative profit</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> (e.g., heavy discounts eroding margins).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>&gt;&gt; Categories with </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>moderate sales but strong profit</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> (efficient pricing or cost control).
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>This helps managers decide whether to adjust pricing, reduce discounts, or focus on profitable products.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.00141044'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.747956'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.510578'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
          <annotation class='area' id='1' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>How to Create a Chart to Analyze Profit by Sub‑Category
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>&#10;1. </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Open a Worksheet</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> in Tableau.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>2. Drag Sub‑Category → Rows shelf</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> (this lists all product sub‑categories vertically).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>3. Drag Profit → Columns shelf</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> (this defines the horizontal axis with profit values).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>4. Tableau will automatically apply </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>SUM(Profit)</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> as the aggregation.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>5. Format the chart:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Turn on </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Data Labels</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> to show exact profit values.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Sort sub‑categories by profit (descending) to highlight top and bottom performers.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Optionally, apply </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>color coding</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> (green for positive profit, red for negative) for clarity.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.507757'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.745913'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.928068'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
        </annotations>
      </table>
      <simple-id uuid='{5BAB43BB-754A-4830-A3EC-1A06DB127C4C}' />
    </worksheet>
    <worksheet name='Q5'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Q5.  Create a Line Chart to show Sales Trend over Order Date. </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Which date level would you choose (Year / Quarter / Month)? </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Why are line charts suitable for time-based analysis?</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Sample - Superstore' name='federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30'>
            <column datatype='date' name='[Order Date]' role='dimension' type='ordinal' />
            <column datatype='real' name='[Sales]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[Order Date]' derivation='Month' name='[mn:Order Date:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
            <column-instance column='[Sales]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:Sales:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
          </datasource-dependencies>
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style />
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Line' />
            <mark-sizing mark-sizing-setting='marks-scaling-off' />
            <encodings>
              <text column='[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[sum:Sales:qk]' />
            </encodings>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='mark'>
                <format attr='mark-labels-show' value='true' />
                <format attr='mark-labels-cull' value='true' />
                <format attr='size' value='1.2413811683654785' />
              </style-rule>
            </style>
          </pane>
        </panes>
        <rows>[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[sum:Sales:qk]</rows>
        <cols>[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[mn:Order Date:ok]</cols>
      </table>
      <simple-id uuid='{4BCF957D-52E4-491D-AA6A-4BD1234AF769}' />
    </worksheet>
    <worksheet name='Q5 '>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Q5.  Create a Line Chart to show Sales Trend over Order Date. </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>(a)Which date level would you choose (Year / Quarter / Month)? </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>(b)Why are line charts suitable for time-based analysis?</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources />
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style />
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Automatic' />
          </pane>
        </panes>
        <rows />
        <cols />
        <annotations>
          <annotation class='area' id='0' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontsize='26'>(a)</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='26'>Which date level would you choose (Year / Quarter / Month)?</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.00292826'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.10981'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
          <annotation class='area' id='1' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Best Choice: Month</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Year shows only broad annual totals (too high‑level).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Quarter gives seasonal patterns but still coarse.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Month reveals detailed trends</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> (seasonality, monthly spikes, dips).</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.103953'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.323572'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
          <annotation class='area' id='2' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>(b)Why are line charts suitable for time-based analysis?</run>
              <run fontsize='24'>Æ </run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.301611'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.445095'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
          <annotation class='area' id='3' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Line charts emphasize </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>continuity over time</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>They clearly show </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>trends, growth, decline, and seasonality</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Easy to spot </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>patterns</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> like holiday spikes, year‑end drops, or steady growth.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Unlike bar charts, line charts highlight the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>flow of data across time intervals</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.000681199'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.442167'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.999319'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.685212'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
        </annotations>
      </table>
      <simple-id uuid='{2625874A-0708-4E14-AE86-C9544D477378}' />
    </worksheet>
    <worksheet name='Q6'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Q6.  Apply a Basic Filter to display data only for: Region = “West” Category = “Technology” 
Explain the steps and mention which shelf is used.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>&gt;&gt; Open your worksheet in Tableau with the </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Sample – Superstore</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> dataset.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>&gt;&gt; n the </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Data Pane</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> (left side), locate the field </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Region</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>&gt;&gt; Drag </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Region → Filters Shelf</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;In the filter dialog box, select </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>West</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>&gt;&gt; Next, locate the field </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Category</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>&gt;&gt; Drag </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Category → Filters Shelf</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>&gt;&gt; In the filter dialog box, select </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Technology</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>&gt;&gt; Click </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>OK</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>. Tableau will now restrict the view to only records where </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Region = West</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> and </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>&gt;&gt; </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Category = Technology</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Which Shelf Is Used?</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>The </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Filters Shelf</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> is used to apply these restrictions.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>This shelf controls which subset of data is displayed in the visualization.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Sample - Superstore' name='federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30'>
            <column datatype='string' name='[Category]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
            <column datatype='string' name='[Region]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
            <column datatype='real' name='[Sales]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[Category]' derivation='None' name='[none:Category:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
            <column-instance column='[Region]' derivation='None' name='[none:Region:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
            <column-instance column='[Sales]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:Sales:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
          </datasource-dependencies>
          <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[none:Category:nk]'>
            <groupfilter function='member' level='[none:Category:nk]' member='&quot;Technology&quot;' user:ui-domain='database' user:ui-enumeration='inclusive' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
          </filter>
          <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[none:Region:nk]'>
            <groupfilter function='member' level='[none:Region:nk]' member='&quot;West&quot;' user:ui-domain='database' user:ui-enumeration='inclusive' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
          </filter>
          <slices>
            <column>[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[none:Region:nk]</column>
            <column>[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[none:Category:nk]</column>
          </slices>
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style />
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Automatic' />
            <encodings>
              <text column='[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[sum:Sales:qk]' />
            </encodings>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='mark'>
                <format attr='mark-labels-show' value='true' />
                <format attr='mark-labels-cull' value='true' />
              </style-rule>
            </style>
          </pane>
        </panes>
        <rows>[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[none:Category:nk]</rows>
        <cols>[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[sum:Sales:qk]</cols>
      </table>
      <simple-id uuid='{BFB2852A-010F-40C1-82F4-BD1AF2279AF2}' />
    </worksheet>
    <worksheet name='Q7'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Q7. Explain the business importance of geographical analysis. Then describe how you would create a Map showing Sales by State using Sample – Superstore.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources />
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style />
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Automatic' />
          </pane>
        </panes>
        <rows />
        <cols />
        <annotations>
          <annotation class='area' id='0' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Business Importance of Geographical Analysis</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>1. Regional Performance Tracking</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> → Helps businesses see which states or regions drive the most sales.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>2. Market Expansion Decisions</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> → Identifies untapped or underperforming areas for growth.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>3. Resource Allocation</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> → Guides where to invest marketing, inventory, or manpower.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>4. Customer Insights</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> → Reveals location‑based buying patterns and preferences.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>5. Risk Management</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> → Detects regions with declining sales or negative profit trends.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.011782'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.405007'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
          <annotation class='area' id='1' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Steps to Create a Map Showing Sales by State (Sample – Superstore)
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>&gt;&gt; Open a Worksheet</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> in Tableau.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>&gt;&gt; Drag </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>State → Rows shelf</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> (or directly onto the canvas).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>&gt;&gt; Drag </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Sales → Columns shelf</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> (or directly onto the canvas).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>&gt;&gt; Tableau will automatically generate a </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Map view</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> because “State” is a geographical field.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>&gt;&gt; By default, Tableau applies </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>SUM(Sales)</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> as the aggregation.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>&gt;Format the map:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>&gt;&gt; Use </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Color</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> on Sales to shade states by sales volume.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>&gt;&gt; Add </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Labels</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> to show exact sales values.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Adjust the map style (filled map or symbol map) for clarity</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.407953'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.904271'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
        </annotations>
      </table>
      <simple-id uuid='{D010A046-DFE6-4323-AD40-3D21648EFB27}' />
    </worksheet>
    <worksheet name='Q7 '>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Q7. Explain the business importance of geographical analysis. Then describe how you would create a Map showing Sales by State using Sample – Superstore.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Sample - Superstore' name='federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30' />
          </datasources>
          <mapsources>
            <mapsource name='Tableau' />
          </mapsources>
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30'>
            <column datatype='string' name='[Country]' role='dimension' semantic-role='[Country].[ISO3166_2]' type='nominal' />
            <column datatype='real' name='[Sales]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column datatype='string' name='[State]' role='dimension' semantic-role='[State].[Name]' type='nominal' />
            <column-instance column='[Country]' derivation='None' name='[none:Country:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
            <column-instance column='[State]' derivation='None' name='[none:State:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
            <column-instance column='[Sales]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:Sales:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
          </datasource-dependencies>
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style>
          <style-rule element='map'>
            <format attr='washout' value='0.0' />
          </style-rule>
        </style>
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Multipolygon' />
            <encodings>
              <color column='[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[none:State:nk]' />
              <text column='[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[none:State:nk]' />
              <text column='[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[sum:Sales:qk]' />
              <lod column='[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[none:Country:nk]' />
              <geometry column='[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[Geometry (generated)]' />
            </encodings>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='mark'>
                <format attr='mark-labels-show' value='true' />
                <format attr='mark-labels-cull' value='true' />
              </style-rule>
            </style>
          </pane>
        </panes>
        <rows>[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[Latitude (generated)]</rows>
        <cols>[federated.16t1epn0d8xkkr17i5uvi1iouw30].[Longitude (generated)]</cols>
      </table>
      <simple-id uuid='{B7296017-1B55-4061-A1CF-9378DCA98A8A}' />
    </worksheet>
    <worksheet name='Q8'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Q8. What is the difference between a Worksheet and a Dashboard in Tableau? Why is a dashboard more useful for decision-makers?</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources />
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style />
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Automatic' />
          </pane>
        </panes>
        <rows />
        <cols />
        <annotations>
          <annotation class='area' id='0' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Difference Between Worksheet and Dashboard in Tableau</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.0883652'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
          <annotation class='area' id='1' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Worksheet</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>A single view where you build </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>one visualization</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> (bar chart, line chart, map, etc.).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Contains </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Rows, Columns, Marks card, Filters</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>, and the data pane.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Best for creating and analyzing </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>individual charts</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>.&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Dashboard</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>A </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>collection of multiple worksheets</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> combined into one interactive view.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Can include charts, maps, text boxes, images, and filters.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Best for providing a </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>holistic overview</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> of data.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.0810015'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.444772'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
          <annotation class='area' id='2' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Why Dashboards Are More Useful for Decision‑Makers</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.441826'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.537555'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
          <annotation class='area' id='3' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>1. Consolidated View</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> → Dashboards show KPIs, charts, and maps all in one place.
</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>2. Interactivity</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> → Filters and actions allow decision‑makers to drill down into details.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>&#10;3.Comparison</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> → Multiple metrics can be compared side‑by‑side (e.g., Sales vs Profit vs Region).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>&#10;4. Efficiency</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> → Saves time by avoiding switching between multiple worksheets.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>&#10;5. Storytelling</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'> → Dashboards highlight trends and insights in a way that supports quick, informed decisions.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.530191'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.889543'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
        </annotations>
      </table>
      <simple-id uuid='{45D85299-7BC9-43AE-8EC9-9702C9AA8B07}' />
    </worksheet>
    <worksheet name='Q9'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Q9.  What is Tableau Prep, and why is it important in real-world data projects? 
What is Tableau Prep, and why is it important in real-world data projects? 
Then explain how you would: Remove null values Remove duplicate records Change incorrect data types (Answer in steps, no tool access required.)</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources />
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style />
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Automatic' />
          </pane>
        </panes>
        <rows />
        <cols />
        <annotations>
          <annotation class='area' id='0' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#e15759' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>What is Tableau Prep?</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Tableau Prep</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> is a data preparation tool from Tableau.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>It helps users </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>clean, shape, and combine data</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> before analysis.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Instead of working with messy raw data, Prep allows you to:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Remove errors and inconsistencies.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Standardize formats.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Join multiple datasets.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Create flows that can be reused for automation.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.291457'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
          <annotation class='area' id='1' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#f28e2b' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Importance in Real‑World Data Projects</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>1. Data Quality</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> → Ensures dashboards are built on accurate, reliable data.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>2. Efficiency</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> → Saves analysts time by automating repetitive cleaning tasks.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>3. Scalability</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> → Handles large, complex datasets from multiple sources.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>4. Consistency</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> → Standardizes data preparation across teams.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>5. Decision‑Making</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> → Clean data leads to trustworthy insights for managers.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.279732'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.504188'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
          <annotation class='area' id='2' text-pinx='0.5' text-piny='0.5' text-width-delta='-18'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#f28e2b' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Steps to Perform Common Cleaning Tasks</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>1. Remove Null Values</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Open your data in Tableau Prep.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Identify columns with </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>null/blank values</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Use the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Filter option</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> → Exclude nulls.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Alternatively, replace nulls with default values (e.g., 0 for numbers, “Unknown” for text).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>2. Remove Duplicate Records</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>In the Prep workspace, select the table.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Use the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Remove Duplicates option</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> (or group by unique keys like Order ID).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Tableau Prep will keep only unique rows.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>3. Change Incorrect Data Types</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>In the field list, check each column’s data type (Text, Number, Date).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>If incorrect (e.g., Order Date stored as Text):</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Click the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>data type icon</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> next to the field name.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Change it to the correct type (Date, Integer, String, etc.).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>This ensures calculations and visualizations work properly.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <top-left>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.497487'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </top-left>
            <bottom-right>
              <visual-coordinate class='axis'>
                <x-coord cell-offset='0.998638'>
                  <node-reference />
                </x-coord>
                <y-coord cell-offset='0.998325'>
                  <node-reference />
                </y-coord>
                <page-reference />
              </visual-coordinate>
            </bottom-right>
            <text x='0.5' y='0.5' />
          </annotation>
        </annotations>
      </table>
      <simple-id uuid='{0A541C9D-73B8-48D4-A8CA-73EF1465B6A0}' />
    </worksheet>
